{{Infobox
| Box title=Glyph
| image=SampleInGameGlyph.jpg
| caption=Glyph as seen in-game (code: WARFRAMEWIKI)
}}
'''Glyphs''' are [[wikipedia:Pin Art|pin-table]] style icons that can be placed on surfaces during missions to display a pre-selected image and also serve as player icons/avatars in the game.

{{toclimit|3}}

==Changing your Glyph==
You can change your equipped glyph by opening the pause menu, selecting '''Profile''', then selecting '''Glyph.'''
==Default Glyphs==
These Glyphs are unlocked by default:
{{GlyphBox|ExcaliburGlyph.png|Excalibur Glyph}}
{{GlyphBox|LotusSymbolGlyph.png|Lotus Symbol Glyph}}
{{GlyphBox|RhinoGlyph.png|Rhino Glyph}}
{{GlyphBox|TrinityGlyph.png|Trinity Glyph}}
{{GlyphBox|VoltGlyph.png|Volt Glyph}}

Although these Glyphs are not unlocked by default, they share the same design and can be purchased for {{pc|10}} each.

{{GlyphBox|AshGlyph.png|Ash Glyph}}
{{GlyphBox|EmberGlyph.png|Ember Glyph}}
{{GlyphBox|LokiGlyph.png|Loki Glyph}}
{{GlyphBox|MagGlyph.png|Mag Glyph}}

==Normal Glyphs==
These Glyphs depict Warframes and their Alternate Helmets with a light/dark background. They can be purchased for {{pc|10}} each. Purchasing one version will not unlock the other.

